  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member who picks the « REDFACE 3D Big » app icon, I want the Home Screen to show the icon I saw in the picker (black rim around the red face), so that the choice is not a surprise. Today the picker (Réglages, dark appearance) shows the black rim, while the Home Screen (light appearance) shows the face on a red background. Operator: **the black-rim one is the real icon**.\n\n### Cause (not settled)\n\nWhat the repo shows (`dev-swift` 64c14d4f):\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Icon-RedFace3DBig.icon/icon.json` is a layered Icon Composer file whose background `fill` is an `automatic-gradient` of red (`display-p3:0.66777,0.00619,0,1`), identical to the legacy file (`SuperHFRplus/Assets/AlternativeIcons/Icon-RedFace3DBig.icon/icon.json` @ `87fe0d1c`).\n- The picker previews of #809 (`Assets.xcassets/IconPreviews/IconPreview-Icon-RedFace3DBig.imageset`) differ by appearance: `default.png` red rim, `dark.png` black rim. The picker seen in dark appearance therefore shows the black rim.\n\nWhat the device shows (operator, 2026-11-13): the Home Screen icon is red-rimmed, and **stays red-rimmed after switching the iPhone to dark mode**. So the light/dark split of the file does not explain it on its own. To check on the Mac and the device, in this order:\n1. The Home Screen's own icon style (Home Screen › Edit › Customize: Default, Dark, Clear, Tinted): with Default the icons may stay light whatever the system appearance.\n2. Whether an alternate `.icon` set with `setAlternateIconName` keeps its dark variant once compiled (`actool` output in the built app's `Assets.car`), or only the default one.\n3. How the `dark.png` preview was produced in #809, and whether it matches anything the system draws for this icon.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Make « REDFACE 3D Big » black-rimmed in every appearance (light, dark, and tinted/clear as far as the format allows): a dark background fill instead of the red automatic gradient, the face layers unchanged.\n- Regenerate its two previews so both show the black rim.\n- Check the other `.icon` files of the picker for the same light/dark split, and list any that has it on this issue (fix only on the operator's call).\n- An intentional difference from legacy (`87fe0d1c` draws the red rim in light): note it in the PR's `### Ledger` section.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On a device in light appearance, the Home Screen icon has the black rim, like the picker.\n- [ ] In dark appearance, unchanged (black rim).\n- [ ] Both previews of `IconPreview-Icon-RedFace3DBig` show the black rim.\n- [ ] Other icons with a light/dark split are listed here.\n\nRelated: #730 / #809 (icon packs and previews), #731 (LOT-190 icon art, PR #805), #580 (the port of the layered icon).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n\n",
