   "updated_at": "2026-11-19T05:42:03Z",
   "body": "**Simulator check (mac/M1, 2026-11-19, `dev-swift` 71a05c41).** The device check is replaced by a simulator check (operator, 2026-11-18).\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `icon.json` of REDFACE 3D Big | One near-black fill (`display-p3:0.03137,0.03137,0.03137`) for the default, dark and tinted appearances (#805, `01ed22a6`). |\n| Compiled `Assets.car` (`assetutil`) | The alternate `Icon-RedFace3DBig` keeps its light, dark and tinted renditions (`IconImageStack` × 3, 1024 px `Icon Image` × 3), exactly like the primary icon `Icon-RedFace3D`. Checks 1 and 2 of the \"Cause\" section: the compiled alternate icon does not lose its variants. |\n| Home Screen, light appearance (iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.2) | Black rim around the red face, like the picker. |\n| Home Screen, dark appearance | Black rim. The simulator's Home Screen stays on the Default icon style: the system icons (Calendrier, Plans) also stay light. A device on Default may likewise show the light variant whatever the system appearance; that variant is now black-rimmed too. |\n| Picker preview `IconPreview-Icon-RedFace3DBig` | #805 replaced the old default/dark pair with one image for every appearance. It has the black rim. |\n| Other `.icon` files with a light/dark split (criterion 4) | None has a background fill that differs between appearances. The 23 bundles of #805 (Beta Red, Classique Blue, Halloween ×2, Noël ×2, Orange, Saisons ×3, X-face ×11) show a separate default, dark or tinted layer through `hidden-specializations`: a dark artwork by design (ICONS.md), not this bug. `Icon-RedFace3D` and `Icon-RedFace3DBig` change only the opacity of the left eye in dark (1 → 0.5 and 0.7 → 0.5), as in legacy. |\n\nMethod: the Home Screen was captured with the app built with `ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME=Icon-RedFace3DBig`. That is the same `actool` compilation as the alternate icon. I tried setting the alternate icon through `setAlternateIconName` from a hosted test, but the test run hung (Mac swap full) and I stopped it. The tinted and clear styles cannot be set from `simctl`, so they were not seen.\n\nClosing per AGENTS §8: the fix shipped in #805.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
